root = TaxonomyBrowser(
  "Steps vs Understanding",
  [proceduralKnowledge, conceptualKnowledge, transfer],
)

proceduralKnowledge = TaxonomyCategory(
  "Procedural Knowledge",
  "Knowing the steps",
  "ListOrdered",
  "yellow",
  "Procedural knowledge is knowing the steps; it breaks as soon as the user's situation differs from the documented one.",
  "A user who has memorised 'Select Share, enter the e-mail, select Send' can share a file exactly as the manual shows. But when the Share button is greyed out, or the person is outside the company, they are stuck: the steps don't say what to do and they have nothing else to reason with. Procedural knowledge is necessary, but it's brittle.",
  "Knowing the bus route by heart: perfect until a road is closed.",
  "Doing the documented task",
  ["Memorised steps and click paths", "Tasks exactly as documented"],
  ["Situations the manual didn't foresee"],
)

conceptualKnowledge = TaxonomyCategory(
  "Conceptual Knowledge",
  "Knowing what, how it relates, and why",
  "Network",
  "green",
  "Conceptual knowledge is knowing what the parts are, how they relate and why, which lets users work out steps nobody documented.",
  "A user who understands that 'sharing is controlled by the workspace's permission settings, and external sharing is off by default' can reason about the greyed-out button themselves: check the workspace settings, or ask the admin. Conceptual knowledge is the map; procedural knowledge is one route across it.",
  "Knowing the city map, so you can find a new route when a road is closed.",
  "Reasoning about the system",
  ["What the parts are and how they relate", "Why the system behaves as it does"],
  ["Memorised click paths"],
)

transfer = TaxonomyCategory(
  "Transfer",
  "Using it in a new situation",
  "Shuffle",
  "sky",
  "Transfer is applying what you learned to a new situation; conceptual knowledge is what makes transfer possible.",
  "No manual can document every situation: every combination of role, data and setting. Transfer is the real goal of teaching: the user meets a case the docs never showed and still acts correctly. Steps alone rarely transfer; an understood idea does.",
  "Learning to cook rather than learning one recipe.",
  "Acting correctly in undocumented situations",
  ["New combinations of roles, data and settings", "Features added after training"],
  ["Repeating the exact example from the manual"],
)
